    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm a freelance designer and i'm trying to clean up my quickbooks for the year. i just bought a really expensive ergonomic chair for my home studio setup. do i categorize that as a business expense or is it a personal draw? i'm a bit confused about how the irs views home office equipment.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You can generally deduct the purchase of a chair if you use it exclusively and regularly for business, but you must allocate the cost based on how much of your time you spend working in that specific area versus personal use. Since home office rules have tightened significantly this year due to increased remote work cases, the IRS likely requires you to calculate a percentage of your time spent in the designated workspace and prorate the deduction accordingly. For tax purposes, this would be considered a business expense rather than a personal draw, provided you keep detailed records of your setup and usage times.",
