      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The \"exclusive use\" rule applies to the specific area of your office, not necessarily every single minute of the chair's life if your gaming session is short and targeted; however, if you often alternate between working and gaming extensively, the IRS may require you to prorate the deduction based on usable space rather than time alone. If your gaming becomes a significant portion of your time there, you might need to document that the space is still primarily dedicated to business, or consider allocating a larger percentage to your personal draw. Furthermore, missing a receipt for smaller equipment matters less to your average deduction than for high-value items like your chair, provided you have your credit card statement and can reasonably explain the expense's nature for audit trails.",
